RAR decoding on Android, iOS, macOS, Linux, and Windows uses the official UnRAR
sources. Those sources may be used to handle RAR archives without limitations
free of charge, but cannot be used to develop a RAR-compatible archiver or to
re-create the RAR compression algorithm, which is proprietary. Copyright
remains with Alexander Roshal. See src/UNRAR_LICENSE.txt.

Web listing uses the koni_archive packages, which keep their own license.
This package does not include the proprietary RAR compression algorithm and
cannot create RAR archives.
